{"id":"b020503ba5d16dce","group":"88","path":"88/88-df-partial-computable.md","title":"Partial Computable Function","display":"df-partial-computable — Partial Computable Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Computability and Logic","book_abbrev":"88","label":"88-df-partial-computable","aliases":["88-df-partial-computable"],"display":"df-partial-computable — Partial Computable Function","depends_on":["[[88-df-computable-function]]","[[88-df-partial-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Computability and Logic"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"88"},{"key":"label","html":"88-df-partial-computable"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>88-df-partial-computable</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-partial-computable — Partial Computable Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64279ecae5246baf\" href=\"?note=64279ecae5246baf\" title=\"88-df-computable-function\">88-df-computable-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d585cbf989199162\" href=\"?note=d585cbf989199162\" title=\"88-df-partial-function\">88-df-partial-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> (arity)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\">\\(\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\\)</span> (partial function, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d585cbf989199162\" href=\"?note=d585cbf989199162\" title=\"88-df-partial-function\">88-df-partial-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Comp}(f)\">\\(\\mathrm{Comp}(f)\\)</span> (computability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"64279ecae5246baf\" href=\"?note=64279ecae5246baf\" title=\"88-df-computable-function\">88-df-computable-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\">\\(\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\\)</span> (class of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-ary partial computable functions)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartComp}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartComp}\\)</span> (partial computable function class)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}partial\\text{-}computable} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\n\\coloneqq\n\\{f:\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\\land\\mathrm{Comp}(f)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}partial\\text{-}computable} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\n\\coloneqq\n\\{f:\\mathrm{PartialFunction}(f,\\mathbb N^k,\\mathbb N)\\land\\mathrm{Comp}(f)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}partial\\text{-}computable} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PartComp}\\coloneqq\\bigcup_{k\\in\\mathbb N}\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}partial\\text{-}computable} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{PartComp}\\coloneqq\\bigcup_{k\\in\\mathbb N}\\mathrm{PartComp}_k\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartComp}_1\">\\(\\mathrm{PartComp}_1\\)</span> is the unary class used by Rice's theorem and its index sets.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PartComp}\">\\(\\mathrm{PartComp}\\)</span> is the union over all finite arities.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","l